{"status":"complete","verdict":"Ready with fixes","verdict_reasoning":"One confirmed, reproduced P1 (#1) is open: parseBody() after c.req.formData() now throws a 500 on multipart or returns garbage keys on urlencoded, a regression from the base commit on a public API path, so the verdict is capped at Ready with fixes. The case-insensitive media-type fix itself is correct and fully tested against issue #5060. Fix order: #1 first (reuse bodyCache.formData before reading bytes, mirroring validator.ts:115-121), and while editing that branch publish bodyCache.formData before the first await to close the confirmed P3 race (#2); add the formData()->parseBody() ordering and Promise.all tests named in the findings.","fix_order":[1,2],"scope":{"base":"9728702911073aec5a63a3ba2840b7240e5d3205","branch":"review-head","head_sha":"5226d4165d48643586152614cbd07422a0ab7a22","pr_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5067","pr_number":5067,"mode":"standalone","files_changed":6,"files":["src/utils/body.test.ts","src/utils/body.ts","src/utils/buffer.test.ts","src/utils/buffer.ts","src/validator/validator.test.ts","src/validator/validator.ts"]},"intent":"Make Hono's body parsing and validator match Content-Type media types case-insensitively (fixes #5060), so requests such as `Application/JSON` or `Multipart/Form-Data; boundary=...` are parsed and validated instead of silently yielding `{}`. parseBody() now compares the lowercased media type (part before `;`) and reads the raw body via arrayBuffer() + bufferToFormData() (which lowercases only the media type, preserving parameters such as the boundary), caching the resulting FormData promise on HonoRequest.bodyCache; the validator's JSON/multipart/urlencoded regexes gain the /i flag. Must not regress existing body-cache behaviour (interplay of c.req.parseBody(), c.req.formData(), c.req.json()/text()/arrayBuffer(), validator('form'), cloneRawRequest) or multipart boundary handling.","intent_confidence":"explicit","reviewers":["correctness","testing","security","adversarial"],"findings":[{"#":1,"title":"parseBody() breaks when c.req.formData() was called first","severity":"P1","file":"src/utils/body.ts","line":126,"confidence":100,"autofix_class":"gated_auto","owner":"downstream-resolver","requires_verification":true,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"In parseFormData, reuse an existing cached FormData before reading bytes, mirroring src/validator/validator.ts:115-121:

```ts
async function parseFormData<T extends BodyData>(request: HonoRequest | Request, options: ParseBodyOptions): Promise<T> {
  let formData: FormData
  if (request instanceof HonoRequest && request.bodyCache.formData) {
    formData = await request.bodyCache.formData
  } else {
    const headers = request instanceof HonoRequest ? request.raw.headers : request.headers
    const arrayBuffer = await (request as Request).arrayBuffer()
    const formDataPromise = bufferToFormData(arrayBuffer, headers.get('Content-Type') || '')
    if (request instanceof HonoRequest) {
      request.bodyCache.formData = formDataPromise as unknown as FormData
    }
    formData = await formDataPromise
  }
  if (formData) {
    return convertFormDataToBodyData<T>(formData, options)
  }
  return {} as T
}
```

